WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.330
NARRATOR: Great whites
grow up to 20 feet long,

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.060
and can pack over
5,000 pounds of muscle.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.390
Yet, despite their size,
they often go unnoticed.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.160
A type of camouflage
known as counter shading

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.950
gives these sharks
the predatory edge.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.970
They're dark on top,
but pale underneath.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:43.060
So underwater, they blend
into the background,

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.830
whether seen from
above or below.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.670
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:57.250
But all that changes
from the air.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.180
ANDY: All right.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.210
Here we go, tethered
drone taking off.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.350
NARRATOR: From high
in the sky, a shark's

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:14.660
camouflage can't hide them,
and their cover will be blown.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.450
ANDY: Let's try to
find some sharks here.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:26.810
NARRATOR: The best view of
what's below the surface

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.750
comes from high above.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.390
Andy' drone scans from the sky.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.220
And while down at
water level, it

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:47.310
looks like every other
day at the beach, the view

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.344
from above--

00:01:49.344 --> 00:01:50.735
 Woah, woah, right there.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.000
NARRATOR: Reveals a
very different story.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:07.840
A drone's eye view detects
an unmistakable silhouette.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.515
Now you see it, now you don't.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.760
ANDY: It's pretty incredible.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.300
There's sharks everywhere
literally right

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.390
under the boards of
these people, right

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.020
under their noses, and
they don't even see it.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:32.070
NARRATOR: Down at water
level, glare and reflections

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:37.770
can easily distract hiding what
looks obvious from high above.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.193
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.390
ANDY: I got a lot of
sharks in the area.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.950
This is incredible.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.590
NARRATOR: It looks
too close for comfort.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.195
But are people in danger?

00:02:52.195 --> 00:02:56.286
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:02.940
Despite Santa Barbara's
increase in shark sightings,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.550
there hasn't been a
fatal shark bite here

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:11.010
in almost a decade,
a stat that today's

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.675
survey will help unpack.

00:03:12.675 --> 00:03:17.670
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.770
ANDY: Synchronize watches.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.900
All right, great white
stakeout, here we go.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:27.490
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.860
All right, and 3,
2, 1, here we go.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.910
[MUSIC PLAYING]

